    "title": "Man to be sentenced in November in connection to teen's death in Albuquerque - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ALBUQUERQUE, N.M. (KRQE) – A man who admitted taking part in the murder of a 13-year-old a year ago will be sentenced for his crimes in November. Michael Flores pleaded guilty to conspiracy and evidence tampering charges in February. He admitted to driving around with Thomas Acee when they fired off shots near 5th St. and Coal Ave., killing 13-year-old Michael Tubb and injuring another teen. Flores agreed to testify against Acee as part of his plea deal, but Acee died in late July. The court set a sentencing date for November 13. He’s facing up to 20 years behind bars. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.",
